# Known Issues

This file tracks known bugs, limitations, and deferred work items for the project.

## How to Use

- **Before working on a component**: Check this file for known problems
  that may affect your work or that your work could address.
- **When discovering a new issue**: Add an entry with status, date, component,
  problem description, and any known root cause or workaround.
- **When resolving an issue**: Update the status to "Resolved" with the date and
  a brief note on the fix, but keep the entry for historical context.

## Current Open Issues

- **ML Table Detection underperforms heuristic** -- `MLTableDetection/TableDetectorML.py`
  exists and has been trained through four iterations (v2, v4, v5, v5b). The best model
  (v4) averages mAP@0.5 = 0.47 across 5 held-out PDFs (best:
  `Electrical_Takeoff_page7=1.00`; previously-documented headline:
  `generic3=0.66`; worst: `K=0.13`). See the
  "v4 held-out baseline -- DONE 2026-05-07" entry below for the full
  per-PDF table. v4 still trails the heuristic `PanelSearchToolV25`
  which finds all 6 panels on generic3. Adding negative examples
  (v5, v5b) caused regressions. v4 remains the best Table Transformer
  model.
  **Root cause identified (2026-05-06)**: dataset size is the primary bottleneck.
  Microsoft Table Transformer maintainers recommend ~1,000 images as the
  fine-tuning floor (per [microsoft/table-transformer Issue #108](https://github.com/microsoft/table-transformer/issues/108));
  the original `annotations_coco.json` had only 28 images with annotations.
  See "Dataset expansion (Phase 1) -- DONE" entry below for the v6 dataset and
  the "Phase 2 audit gaps -- DONE" entry for the training-script changes.
  Evaluation infrastructure already exists at `MLTableDetection/evaluate_model.py`
  (modes: `--data` for COCO mAP, `--images` for inference, `--pdf` for
  box-level ML-vs-heuristic comparison with mAP / precision / recall / mean IoU).

- **Dataset expansion (Phase 1) -- DONE 2026-05-06** -- A 298-image / 821-annotation
